+Round 24 carries two corrections and changes no prompt body and no contract. `F1`, raised by
+the independent §10 review of round 23 and accepted without argument: round 23 shipped
+`SF10-09`'s validation behaviour while still emitting `validator_revision: 3.2.8`, the
+identity round 22's report on `main` already records measurements against from different
+bytes. The counts coincided and that coincidence was the hazard, so `validator_revision`
+moves to **3.2.9** at its four sites. Because 3.2.10 is installed and bound to a published
+§10 verdict, corrected bytes must not reuse it, so `FLOWMASTER_VALIDATE_REVISION` moves to
+**3.2.11** in the same change. `SF10-11` closes a coverage gap `D5` concealed: the class-map
+fixture renamed in round 21 tests a *retargeted* CRD destination, and nothing exercised an
+*absent* CRD branch. Two fixtures are added, and falsification decides which: dropping the
+mapping half of `len(rows) != 2 or mapping != expected` leaves only
+`reject-source-epic-to-crd` failing, and dropping the length half leaves only
+`reject-source-duplicate-crd-class-branch` failing. Each half of the guard now has a case
+that uniquely fires it; before this round the length half had none. `change-flow` is untouched and stays at 3.2.8; only this skill's bytes
+move, so only this skill needs a fresh §10.
